# Memory guarantees and allocation evidence

**Measured:** 2026-10-12 · **Source:** [`aaaaaaaaaaaa`](https://github.com/example/fai/tree/aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa) · [Data and reproducibility](https://example.test/evidence)

Perceus is Fai's reference-counting and storage-reuse model. These checks verify ownership, reuse and memory release within Fai.

## Memory guarantees

**All required memory checks passed.**

| Check suite | Tests passed | What it checks |
|---|---:|---|
| Live memory and ownership | 2 | Reference balance, reuse, sharing and resource lifetimes |
| Retained runtime storage | 2 | Bounded allocator storage and release of large buffers |

## Effect of memory optimizations

Arrows mean **optimization disabled → enabled** on the same source and input. Reference counting stays active in both runs. This overview uses each benchmark's largest input.

| Benchmark | Input size | Allocation requests | Extra peak live memory | Retained runtime storage |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Sequence fusion | 100,000 | 1,000 → 0 | 24 B → 24 B | 64 KiB → 64 KiB |
| Scalar replacement | 4,096 | 1,000 → 0 | 24 B → 24 B | 64 KiB → 64 KiB |
| Shared list | 4,096 | 1,000 → 0 | 24 B → 24 B | 64 KiB → 64 KiB |
| Unique list | 4,096 | 1,000 → 0 | 24 B → 24 B | 64 KiB → 64 KiB |

Extra live memory is above the retained harness baseline. Runtime storage includes allocator-owned memory even after its objects are released. Every measured run finishes with its baseline live-object count and live bytes.

