## Measurement details

<details>
<summary>Methods, environment and reproducibility</summary>

Each pair uses identical Fai source, compiler and input; only the named optimization changes. The measurements use an optimized build with allocation counters.

The accounting domain is `fai-object-storage-v1`. Allocation requests include headers and pooled allocations; reset/reuse avoids a request. Live bytes exclude dead recycling cells. Runtime storage includes owned slabs, mappings and system allocations. Host-language temporaries, allocator arenas and OS page rounding are outside these counters. These figures are distinct from whole-process RSS and cross-language memory comparisons.

- **Snapshot:** `fixture-checkpoint`
- **Completed:** 2026-10-12T00:00:01Z
- **Host:** fixture / fixture
- **CPU:** fixture
- **Rust compiler:** fixture
- **Measurement protocol:** `isolated-aot-v2`

[Raw observations, executable identities and reproduction record](https://example.test/evidence)

The evidence includes all inputs, compiler settings, workload versions and implementation notes.

</details>

